=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ VMSOTEL @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt vmsotel @VERSION@ for OpenVMS: host metrics and logs to an OpenTelemetry collector
1 'NOTICE
=prompt vmsotel is distributed under the MIT licence.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [VMSOTEL.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for vmsotel
    Once, as SYSTEM: create the agent's account (default VMSOTEL, with a
    UIC group of its own above MAXSYSGROUP), set the protections, and
    create VMSOTEL$ROOT:[CONF]VMSOTEL.CONF from its example:
    $ @VMSOTEL$ROOT:[COM]VMSOTEL$CONFIGURE
    Set host (the collector) in VMSOTEL$ROOT:[CONF]VMSOTEL.CONF, then:
    $ @VMSOTEL$ROOT:[COM]VMSOTEL_START
    At boot, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (after TCP/IP):
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VMSOTEL$STARTUP.COM
    At shutdown, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSHUTDWN.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VMSOTEL$SHUTDOWN.COM

PRODUCT REMOVE VMSOTEL stops the agent and deassigns VMSOTEL$ROOT and
VMSOTEL$USER; the configuration, the logs and the account are kept.
